elp for education we want this  for all londons we want this for  migrants who come and live with us  um elaine just one final question to you  thank you so much for taking the time  today but just one final question if i  may uh your foreign minister uh has been  speaking and was talking about this  partnership with the uk and said that  rwanda however would not be welcoming  migrant migrants from neighbouring  countries  i wonder if you have any caveats about  who you will and who you won't accept  because  a lot of those migrants coming to the uk  are from places like syria and  afghanistan but they're also from places  like iran and eritrea eritrea a country  closer to you than the uk  will you accept  migrants from all countries or do you  have exceptions  we don't have exceptions migrants are  people  and what we want to do is invest in  people so there will be no  the only exceptions are  because we do have the option to to  reject uh transfer  of people from the uk  uh for instance in cases uh that concern  our national security we will have that  option if uh for instance uh from  information provided by the uk  government that this individual has a  criminal background  then we would  exercise our right to refuse  that individual but it's on a  case-by-case basis but we will accept  migrants from everywhere

